#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/buying-a-train-ticket.ts:16
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Buying a train ticket is easier when you know which details to provide and "
"which questions to ask. You usually need to explain your destination, "
"travel date, preferred departure time, and whether you need a one-way or "
"return ticket.\n"
"\n"
"You may also need to compare routes, understand transfers, reserve a seat, "
"or ask about discounts.\n"
"\n"
"## Start the Conversation\n"
"\n"
"At a ticket counter, you can begin with:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hello, I’d like to buy a ticket, please.”\n"
"- “Could I get a ticket to Berlin?”\n"
"- “I need to travel to Kraków tomorrow.”\n"
"- “I’d like to know the best way to get to Prague.”\n"
"- “Could you help me find a train to Warsaw?”\n"
"\n"
"The ticket agent may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Where are you travelling to?”\n"
"- “When would you like to leave?”\n"
"- “Is that for today?”\n"
"- “What time would you like to travel?”\n"
"- “Do you need a one-way or return ticket?”\n"
"- “How many passengers are travelling?”\n"
"\n"
"You can answer clearly and directly:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’d like a one-way ticket to Gdańsk for tomorrow morning.”\n"
"\n"
"## Say When You Want to Travel\n"
"\n"
"Be as specific as possible about your preferred date and time.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’d like to travel today.”\n"
"- “I need a ticket for tomorrow morning.”\n"
"- “I’d like to leave at around three.”\n"
"- “Is there a train after six?”\n"
"- “What is the earliest train?”\n"
"- “What is the last train tonight?”\n"
"- “I’d prefer to arrive before noon.”\n"
"- “I can travel at any time after five.”\n"
"\n"
"The agent may offer several options:\n"
"\n"
"> “There is a direct train at 9:20 and another at 10:45.”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’ll take the 9:20 train.”\n"
"- “Is there anything earlier?”\n"
"- “What time does the second train arrive?”\n"
"- “Which option is faster?”\n"
"- “Could you check a later train?”\n"
"\n"
"## Choose a One-Way or Return Ticket\n"
"\n"
"A **one-way ticket** covers only the journey to your destination.\n"
"\n"
"A **return ticket** covers the journey to your destination and the journey "
"back.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases:\n"
"\n"
"- “A one-way ticket, please.”\n"
"- “I’d like a return ticket.”\n"
"- “I’m coming back on Sunday.”\n"
"- “Can the return journey be on a different day?”\n"
"- “Is an open return available?”\n"
"- “Is it cheaper to buy a return ticket?”\n"
"\n"
"The agent may ask:\n"
"\n"
"> “When would you like to return?”\n"
"\n"
"You can answer:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’d like to return on Monday evening, preferably after six.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Direct Trains and Transfers\n"
"\n"
"A direct train takes you to your destination without changing trains.\n"
"\n"
"A journey with a transfer requires you to leave one train and board "
"another.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is it a direct train?”\n"
"- “Do I need to change trains?”\n"
"- “How many transfers are there?”\n"
"- “Where do I need to change?”\n"
"- “How much time do I have between trains?”\n"
"- “Is fifteen minutes enough for the connection?”\n"
"- “Will the connecting train wait if the first train is delayed?”\n"
"- “Do I use the same ticket for both trains?”\n"
"\n"
"You may hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “You need to change trains in Poznań.”\n"
"- “There is one transfer.”\n"
"- “You have twenty minutes between trains.”\n"
"- “The direct train is slower but more convenient.”\n"
"- “The faster option requires two changes.”\n"
"\n"
"When comparing routes, think about both travel time and convenience.\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Departure and Arrival Times\n"
"\n"
"Train schedules usually include:\n"
"\n"
"- Departure time\n"
"- Arrival time\n"
"- Journey duration\n"
"- Train number\n"
"- Platform number\n"
"- Number of transfers\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions:\n"
"\n"
"- “What time does the train leave?”\n"
"- “What time does it arrive?”\n"
"- “How long does the journey take?”\n"
"- “Which platform does it leave from?”\n"
"- “What is the train number?”\n"
"- “How early should I arrive?”\n"
"- “Where can I check for platform changes?”\n"
"\n"
"To confirm what you heard, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Did you say the train leaves at 8:15?”\n"
"- “So I arrive at 11:40, correct?”\n"
"- “Was that platform four or platform fourteen?”\n"
"- “Could you write the departure time down for me?”\n"
"\n"
"Confirming numbers is especially useful because times and platform numbers "
"can sound similar.\n"
"\n"
"## Compare Ticket Types\n"
"\n"
"Depending on the railway, several types of tickets may be available.\n"
"\n"
"Common options include:\n"
"\n"
"- Standard ticket\n"
"- First-class ticket\n"
"- Second-class ticket\n"
"- Flexible ticket\n"
"- Non-refundable ticket\n"
"- Off-peak ticket\n"
"- Advance ticket\n"
"- Sleeper ticket\n"
"- Discounted ticket\n"
"\n"
"Questions you can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “What is the cheapest ticket?”\n"
"- “What is the difference between these options?”\n"
"- “Can I change the departure time?”\n"
"- “Is this ticket refundable?”\n"
"- “Can I cancel it?”\n"
"- “Is the ticket valid on any train?”\n"
"- “Do I have to take this specific train?”\n"
"- “Are there any restrictions?”\n"
"\n"
"A cheaper ticket may offer less flexibility.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “This ticket is cheaper, but it is only valid on the 10:30 train and "
"cannot be refunded.”\n"
"\n"
"Before buying, make sure you understand the conditions.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About First and Second Class\n"
"\n"
"Some trains offer different travel classes.\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much is a second-class ticket?”\n"
"- “What is the price for first class?”\n"
"- “What is included in first class?”\n"
"- “Is there much difference between the two?”\n"
"- “Does first class include a meal?”\n"
"- “Is Wi-Fi available in both classes?”\n"
"\n"
"You can choose by saying:\n"
"\n"
"- “Second class is fine, thank you.”\n"
"- “I’ll take the first-class option.”\n"
"- “I’d prefer the cheaper ticket.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Seat Reservations\n"
"\n"
"Some tickets include an assigned seat, while others allow you to sit in any "
"available seat.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is a seat reservation included?”\n"
"- “Do I need to reserve a seat?”\n"
"- “Can I choose my seat?”\n"
"- “Could I have a window seat?”\n"
"- “Could I have an aisle seat?”\n"
"- “Can we sit together?”\n"
"- “Is there a table seat available?”\n"
"- “Is the train likely to be busy?”\n"
"\n"
"The agent may say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Your seat is in carriage seven.”\n"
"- “You are in seat 42.”\n"
"- “The reservation costs extra.”\n"
"- “You can sit in any unreserved seat.”\n"
"- “There are no seats together on that train.”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"> “Could you check the next train to see whether two seats together are "
"available?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Discounts\n"
"\n"
"You may qualify for a reduced fare based on your age, status, railway card, "
"or group size.\n"
"\n"
"Possible discounts include:\n"
"\n"
"- Student discounts\n"
"- Youth discounts\n"
"- Senior discounts\n"
"- Child tickets\n"
"- Family tickets\n"
"- Group tickets\n"
"- Railway-card discounts\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions:\n"
"\n"
"- “Are there any discounts available?”\n"
"- “Is there a student discount?”\n"
"- “Do children need a ticket?”\n"
"- “Is there a cheaper family ticket?”\n"
"- “Do you offer group discounts?”\n"
"- “Can I use my railway card?”\n"
"- “Do I need to show proof of eligibility?”\n"
"\n"
"The agent may ask to see a student card, identification document, or "
"discount card.\n"
"\n"
"## Travel with Luggage, a Bicycle, or a Pet\n"
"\n"
"Additional rules or tickets may apply when travelling with large luggage, "
"bicycles, or animals.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is luggage included in the ticket?”\n"
"- “Is there a luggage limit?”\n"
"- “Where can I store my suitcase?”\n"
"- “Can I take a bicycle on this train?”\n"
"- “Do I need a bicycle reservation?”\n"
"- “Can I travel with a dog?”\n"
"- “Do I need to buy a ticket for my dog?”\n"
"- “Are pets allowed in every carriage?”\n"
"\n"
"You may also ask about accessibility:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is the train wheelchair accessible?”\n"
"- “Is step-free boarding available?”\n"
"- “Can someone help me board the train?”\n"
"- “Is there space for a wheelchair?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Services on the Train\n"
"\n"
"For longer journeys, you may want to know what is available on board.\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is there Wi-Fi on the train?”\n"
"- “Are there power sockets?”\n"
"- “Is there a restaurant carriage?”\n"
"- “Can I buy food on board?”\n"
"- “Is there a toilet on the train?”\n"
"- “Is air conditioning available?”\n"
"- “Is this a sleeper train?”\n"
"- “Are beds or private compartments available?”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand the Price\n"
"\n"
"Before paying, confirm the total price and what it includes.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much is the ticket?”\n"
"- “Is that the total price?”\n"
"- “Does that include the seat reservation?”\n"
"- “Are there any additional fees?”\n"
"- “Is the return journey included?”\n"
"- “Why is this train more expensive?”\n"
"- “Is there a cheaper departure time?”\n"
"\n"
"You can also compare options:\n"
"\n"
"> “The direct train costs more. How much would I save by taking the train "
"with one transfer?”\n"
"\n"
"## Pay for the Ticket\n"
"\n"
"At the counter, the agent may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “How would you like to pay?”\n"
"- “Are you paying by cash or card?”\n"
"- “Would you like a paper or electronic ticket?”\n"
"- “Would you like the receipt?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful answers include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’ll pay by card.”\n"
"- “Can I pay in cash?”\n"
"- “Could I have a paper ticket, please?”\n"
"- “Can you send the ticket to my email?”\n"
"- “Could I have a receipt?”\n"
"- “Where can I find the booking reference?”\n"
"\n"
"After receiving the ticket, check:\n"
"\n"
"- Your name, if required\n"
"- The destination\n"
"- The travel date\n"
"- The departure time\n"
"- The train number\n"
"- The carriage and seat\n"
"- The ticket conditions\n"
"\n"
"## Handle Common Problems\n"
"\n"
"### The preferred train is sold out\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is there another train available?”\n"
"- “What is the next departure?”\n"
"- “Are there seats in first class?”\n"
"- “Can I travel without a seat reservation?”\n"
"- “Could you check a different route?”\n"
"\n"
"### The ticket is too expensive\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is there a cheaper option?”\n"
"- “Would travelling later be less expensive?”\n"
"- “Is the train with a transfer cheaper?”\n"
"- “Are there any discounted tickets left?”\n"
"- “Could I take a slower train?”\n"
"\n"
"### The connection is too short\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is there an option with a longer transfer?”\n"
"- “What happens if I miss the connection?”\n"
"- “Can I use the next train?”\n"
"- “Will my ticket remain valid?”\n"
"\n"
"### Your plans may change\n"
"\n"
"Ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Can I change this ticket later?”\n"
"- “How much does it cost to change it?”\n"
"- “Can I receive a refund?”\n"
"- “What happens if I miss the train?”\n"
"- “Is a flexible ticket available?”\n"
"\n"
"### The train is delayed or cancelled\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Has the train been delayed?”\n"
"- “How long is the delay?”\n"
"- “Has the train been cancelled?”\n"
"- “Can I use this ticket on another train?”\n"
"- “Where can I request a refund?”\n"
"- “Will I miss my connection?”\n"
"- “Can you help me find another route?”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Station Announcements\n"
"\n"
"At the station, you may hear announcements such as:\n"
"\n"
"- “The train has been delayed.”\n"
"- “The platform has changed.”\n"
"- “The train is now departing from platform eight.”\n"
"- “The train has been cancelled.”\n"
"- “This train terminates here.”\n"
"- “Please do not board this train.”\n"
"- “The train is ready for boarding.”\n"
"- “Mind the gap between the train and the platform.”\n"
"\n"
"Check the departure board regularly, because platform numbers may change "
"shortly before departure.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Ticket-Buying Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical conversation may look like this:\n"
"\n"
"> **Traveller:** Hello, I’d like a ticket to Kraków for tomorrow morning.  \n"
"> **Agent:** Certainly. Would you like a one-way or return ticket?  \n"
"> **Traveller:** A return ticket, please. I’d like to come back on Sunday "
"evening.  \n"
"> **Agent:** There is a direct train tomorrow at 9:15. It arrives at 11:50. "
" \n"
"> **Traveller:** Is a seat reservation included?  \n"
"> **Agent:** Yes. Would you prefer a window or aisle seat?  \n"
"> **Traveller:** A window seat, please. How much is the ticket?  \n"
"> **Agent:** The total is 160 złoty.  \n"
"> **Traveller:** Is there a cheaper option?  \n"
"> **Agent:** There is another train at 10:05 with one transfer. It costs "
"125 złoty.  \n"
"> **Traveller:** How long is the transfer?  \n"
"> **Agent:** Twenty-five minutes.  \n"
"> **Traveller:** That sounds fine. I’ll take that option.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Ticket-Buying Formula\n"
"\n"
"When buying a ticket, follow this structure:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Destination:** Say where you want to go.\n"
"2. **Date and time:** Explain when you want to travel.\n"
"3. **Ticket type:** Choose one-way or return.\n"
"4. **Route:** Ask whether the journey is direct.\n"
"5. **Conditions:** Confirm the price, flexibility, and seat reservation.\n"
"6. **Final check:** Repeat the departure time and platform information.\n"
"7. **Payment:** Choose how you want to pay.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’d like a return ticket to Vienna for Friday morning, returning on "
"Sunday evening. I’d prefer a direct train and a window seat.”\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are buying a train ticket at Central Station. The AI "
"ticket agent will help you compare departures, ticket types, routes, and "
"prices.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Explain your destination and preferred travel time.\n"
"- Choose between a one-way and return ticket.\n"
"- Ask whether the journey is direct.\n"
"- Confirm the departure and arrival times.\n"
"- Ask about the price and ticket conditions.\n"
"- Request a seat preference.\n"
"- Respond to one complication, such as a sold-out train, a transfer, or a "
"higher-than-expected price.\n"
"- Confirm the final journey details before paying.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on getting the information you need and checking that you have "
"understood it correctly. Perfect grammar is less important than choosing "
"the correct journey and ticket."
msgstr ""
"Membeli tiket kereta menjadi lebih mudah ketika Anda tahu detail apa yang "
"harus disediakan dan pertanyaan apa yang harus diajukan. Biasanya Anda "
"perlu menjelaskan tujuan, tanggal perjalanan, waktu keberangkatan yang "
"diinginkan, dan apakah Anda memerlukan tiket sekali jalan atau "
"pulang-pergi.\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin juga perlu membandingkan rute, memahami transfer, memesan "
"kursi, atau bertanya tentang diskon.\n"
"\n"
"## Mulai Percakapan\n"
"\n"
"Di loket tiket, Anda dapat memulai dengan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Halo, saya ingin membeli tiket, tolong.”\n"
"- “Bisa saya dapatkan tiket ke Berlin?”\n"
"- “Saya perlu perjalanan ke Kraków besok.”\n"
"- “Saya ingin tahu cara terbaik untuk pergi ke Praha.”\n"
"- “Bisa Anda membantu saya menemukan kereta ke Warsawa?”\n"
"\n"
"Agen tiket mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Ke mana tujuan Anda?”\n"
"- “Kapan Anda ingin berangkat?”\n"
"- “Apakah itu untuk hari ini?”\n"
"- “Jam berapa Anda ingin bepergian?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda memerlukan tiket sekali jalan atau pulang-pergi?”\n"
"- “Berapa banyak penumpang yang bepergian?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda dapat menjawab dengan jelas dan langsung:\n"
"\n"
"> “Saya ingin tiket sekali jalan ke Gdańsk untuk besok pagi.”\n"
"\n"
"## Katakan Kapan Anda Ingin Bepergian\n"
"\n"
"Jelaskan sedetail mungkin tentang tanggal dan waktu yang diinginkan.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya ingin bepergian hari ini.”\n"
"- “Saya perlu tiket untuk besok pagi.”\n"
"- “Saya ingin berangkat sekitar pukul tiga.”\n"
"- “Apakah ada kereta setelah jam enam?”\n"
"- “Apa kereta paling awal?”\n"
"- “Apa kereta terakhir malam ini?”\n"
"- “Saya lebih suka tiba sebelum tengah hari.”\n"
"- “Saya bisa bepergian kapan saja setelah jam lima.”\n"
"\n"
"Agen mungkin menawarkan beberapa opsi:\n"
"\n"
"> “Ada kereta langsung pada pukul 9:20 dan lainnya pada pukul 10:45.”\n"
"\n"
"Anda dapat merespons:\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya akan naik kereta pukul 9:20.”\n"
"- “Apakah ada yang lebih awal?”\n"
"- “Jam berapa kereta kedua tiba?”\n"
"- “Pilihan mana yang lebih cepat?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda memeriksa kereta yang lebih terlambat?”\n"
"\n"
"## Pilih Tiket Sekali Jalan atau Pulang-Pergi\n"
"\n"
"Tiket **sekali jalan** hanya mencakup perjalanan ke tujuan Anda.\n"
"\n"
"Tiket **pulang-pergi** mencakup perjalanan ke tujuan Anda dan perjalanan "
"kembali.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna:\n"
"\n"
"- “Tiket sekali jalan, tolong.”\n"
"- “Saya ingin tiket pulang-pergi.”\n"
"- “Saya akan kembali pada hari Minggu.”\n"
"- “Bisakah perjalanan kembali dilakukan pada hari yang berbeda?”\n"
"- “Apakah tiket open return tersedia?”\n"
"- “Apakah lebih murah membeli tiket pulang-pergi?”\n"
"\n"
"Agen mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"> “Kapan Anda ingin kembali?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda dapat menjawab:\n"
"\n"
"> “Saya ingin kembali pada Senin malam, sebaiknya setelah jam enam.”\n"
"\n"
"## Tanyakan Tentang Kereta Langsung dan Transfer\n"
"\n"
"Kereta langsung membawa Anda ke tujuan tanpa ganti kereta.\n"
"\n"
"Perjalanan dengan transfer mengharuskan Anda meninggalkan satu kereta dan "
"naik kereta lainnya.\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah itu kereta langsung?”\n"
"- “Apakah saya perlu mengganti kereta?”\n"
"- “Berapa banyak transfer yang ada?”\n"
"- “Di mana saya harus berganti?”\n"
"- “Berapa banyak waktu yang saya miliki antara kereta?”\n"
"- “Apakah lima belas menit cukup untuk koneksi?”\n"
"- “Apakah kereta penghubung akan menunggu jika kereta pertama terlambat?”\n"
"- “Apakah saya menggunakan tiket yang sama untuk kedua kereta?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin mendengar:\n"
"\n"
"- “Anda perlu mengganti kereta di Poznań.”\n"
"- “Ada satu transfer.”\n"
"- “Anda memiliki dua puluh menit antara kereta.”\n"
"- “Kereta langsung lebih lambat tetapi lebih nyaman.”\n"
"- “Opsi yang lebih cepat membutuhkan dua pergantian.”\n"
"\n"
"Ketika membandingkan rute, pikirkan tentang waktu perjalanan dan "
"kenyamanan.\n"
"\n"
"## Memahami Waktu Keberangkatan dan Kedatangan\n"
"\n"
"Jadwal kereta biasanya mencakup:\n"
"\n"
"- Waktu keberangkatan\n"
"- Waktu kedatangan\n"
"- Durasi perjalanan\n"
"- Nomor kereta\n"
"- Nomor peron\n"
"- Jumlah transfer\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan berguna:\n"
"\n"
"- “Jam berapa kereta berangkat?”\n"
"- “Jam berapa tiba?”\n"
"- “Berapa lama perjalanan berlangsung?”\n"
"- “Dari peron mana kereta berangkat?”\n"
"- “Apa nomor keretanya?”\n"
"- “Seberapa awal saya harus tiba?”\n"
"- “Di mana saya bisa memeriksa perubahan peron?”\n"
"\n"
"Untuk mengonfirmasi apa yang Anda dengar, katakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah Anda mengatakan kereta berangkat pukul 8:15?”\n"
"- “Jadi saya tiba pukul 11:40, benar?”\n"
"- “Apakah itu peron empat atau peron empat belas?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda menuliskan waktu keberangkatan untuk saya?”\n"
"\n"
"Mengecek ulang angka sangat berguna karena waktu dan nomor peron bisa "
"terdengar mirip.\n"
"\n"
"## Bandingkan Jenis Tiket\n"
"\n"
"Tergantung pada kereta api, beberapa jenis tiket mungkin tersedia.\n"
"\n"
"Pilihan umum meliputi:\n"
"\n"
"- Tiket standar\n"
"- Tiket kelas satu\n"
"- Tiket kelas dua\n"
"- Tiket fleksibel\n"
"- Tiket tidak dapat dikembalikan\n"
"- Tiket off-peak\n"
"- Tiket di muka\n"
"- Tiket tidur\n"
"- Tiket diskon\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan yang bisa Anda ajukan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apa tiket termurah?”\n"
"- “Apa perbedaan antara pilihan ini?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya mengganti waktu keberangkatan?”\n"
"- “Apakah tiket ini dapat dikembalikan?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya membatalkannya?”\n"
"- “Apakah tiket ini berlaku di semua kereta?”\n"
"- “Apakah saya harus naik kereta ini?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada batasan?”\n"
"\n"
"Tiket yang lebih murah mungkin menawarkan lebih sedikit fleksibilitas.\n"
"\n"
"Misalnya:\n"
"\n"
"> “Tiket ini lebih murah, tetapi hanya berlaku pada kereta pukul 10:30 dan "
"tidak dapat dikembalikan.”\n"
"\n"
"Sebelum membeli, pastikan Anda memahami kondisinya.\n"
"\n"
"## Tanyakan Tentang Kelas Pertama dan Kedua\n"
"\n"
"Beberapa kereta menawarkan kelas perjalanan yang berbeda.\n"
"\n"
"Anda bisa bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Berapa harga tiket kelas dua?”\n"
"- “Apa harga untuk kelas satu?”\n"
"- “Apa yang termasuk dalam kelas satu?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada banyak perbedaan antara keduanya?”\n"
"- “Apakah kelas satu termasuk makanan?”\n"
"- “Apakah Wi-Fi tersedia di kedua kelas?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda bisa memilih dengan mengatakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Kelas dua baik, terima kasih.”\n"
"- “Saya akan mengambil opsi kelas satu.”\n"
"- “Saya lebih suka tiket yang lebih murah.”\n"
"\n"
"## Tanyakan Tentang Reservasi Kursi\n"
"\n"
"Beberapa tiket menyertakan kursi yang ditugaskan, sementara yang lain "
"memungkinkan Anda duduk di kursi yang tersedia.\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan berguna meliputi:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah reservasi kursi termasuk?”\n"
"- “Apakah saya perlu memesan kursi?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya memilih kursi saya?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya mendapatkan kursi jendela?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya mendapatkan kursi lorong?”\n"
"- “Bisakah kami duduk bersama?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada kursi meja tersedia?”\n"
"- “Apakah kereta kemungkinan akan sibuk?”\n"
"\n"
"Agen mungkin mengatakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Kursi Anda di gerbong tujuh.”\n"
"- “Anda berada di kursi 42.”\n"
"- “Reservasi biaya tambahan.”\n"
"- “Anda bisa duduk di kursi yang tidak dipesan.”\n"
"- “Tidak ada kursi bersama di kereta itu.”\n"
"\n"
"Anda bisa merespons:\n"
"\n"
"> “Bisakah Anda memeriksa kereta berikutnya untuk melihat apakah dua kursi "
"bersama tersedia?”\n"
"\n"
"## Tanyakan Tentang Diskon\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin memenuhi syarat untuk tarif yang lebih rendah berdasarkan usia "
"Anda, status, kartu kereta api, atau ukuran kelompok.\n"
"\n"
"Diskon yang mungkin termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- Diskon pelajar\n"
"- Diskon pemuda\n"
"- Diskon lansia\n"
"- Tiket anak-anak\n"
"- Tiket keluarga\n"
"- Tiket grup\n"
"- Diskon kartu kereta api\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan berguna:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah ada diskon yang tersedia?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada diskon pelajar?”\n"
"- “Apakah anak-anak memerlukan tiket?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada tiket keluarga yang lebih murah?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda menawarkan diskon kelompok?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya menggunakan kartu kereta api saya?”\n"
"- “Apakah saya perlu menunjukkan bukti kelayakan?”\n"
"\n"
"Agen mungkin meminta untuk melihat kartu pelajar, dokumen identifikasi, "
"atau kartu diskon.\n"
"\n"
"## Bepergian dengan Bagasi, Sepeda, atau Hewan Peliharaan\n"
"\n"
"Aturan tambahan atau tiket mungkin berlaku saat bepergian dengan bagasi "
"besar, sepeda, atau hewan.\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan berguna meliputi:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah bagasi termasuk dalam tiket?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada batasan bagasi?”\n"
"- “Di mana saya dapat menyimpan koper saya?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya membawa sepeda di kereta ini?”\n"
"- “Apakah saya memerlukan reservasi sepeda?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya bepergian dengan anjing?”\n"
"- “Apakah saya perlu membeli tiket untuk anjing saya?”\n"
"- “Apakah hewan peliharaan diizinkan di setiap gerbong?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda juga dapat bertanya tentang aksesibilitas:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah kereta dapat diakses oleh kursi roda?”\n"
"- “Apakah tersedia pintu masuk tanpa tangga?”\n"
"- “Bisakah seseorang membantu saya naik kereta?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada ruang untuk kursi roda?”\n"
"\n"
"## Tanyakan Tentang Layanan di Kereta\n"
"\n"
"Untuk perjalanan yang lebih lama, Anda mungkin ingin tahu apa yang tersedia "
"di dalam kereta.\n"
"\n"
"Anda dapat bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah ada Wi-Fi di kereta?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada soket daya?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada gerbong restoran?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya membeli makanan di dalam kereta?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada toilet di kereta?”\n"
"- “Apakah pendingin udara tersedia?”\n"
"- “Apakah ini kereta tidur?”\n"
"- “Apakah tempat tidur atau kompartemen pribadi tersedia?”\n"
"\n"
"## Memahami Harga\n"
"\n"
"Sebelum membayar, konfirmasi harga total dan apa yang termasuk.\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Berapa harga tiket?”\n"
"- “Apakah itu harga total?”\n"
"- “Apakah itu termasuk reservasi kursi?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada biaya tambahan?”\n"
"- “Apakah perjalanan kembali termasuk?”\n"
"- “Kenapa kereta ini lebih mahal?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada waktu keberangkatan yang lebih murah?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda juga dapat membandingkan opsi:\n"
"\n"
"> “Kereta langsung lebih mahal. Berapa banyak yang saya hemat dengan "
"mengambil kereta dengan satu transfer?”\n"
"\n"
"## Bayar untuk Tiket\n"
"\n"
"Di konter, agen mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bagaimana Anda ingin membayar?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda membayar dengan tunai atau kartu?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda ingin tiket kertas atau elektronik?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda menginginkan tanda terima?”\n"
"\n"
"Jawaban berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya akan bayar dengan kartu.”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya bayar tunai?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya memiliki tiket kertas, tolong?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda mengirimkan tiket ke email saya?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya mendapatkan tanda terima?”\n"
"- “Di mana saya dapat menemukan referensi pemesanan?”\n"
"\n"
"Setelah menerima tiket, periksa:\n"
"\n"
"- Nama Anda, jika diperlukan\n"
"- Tujuan\n"
"- Tanggal perjalanan\n"
"- Waktu keberangkatan\n"
"- Nomor kereta\n"
"- Gerbong dan kursi\n"
"- Kondisi tiket\n"
"\n"
"## Tangani Masalah Umum\n"
"\n"
"### Kereta yang diinginkan sudah habis terjual\n"
"\n"
"Anda bisa bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah ada kereta lain yang tersedia?”\n"
"- “Apa keberangkatan berikutnya?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada kursi di kelas satu?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya bepergian tanpa reservasi kursi?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda memeriksa rute yang berbeda?”\n"
"\n"
"### Tiket terlalu mahal\n"
"\n"
"Anda bisa mengatakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah ada opsi yang lebih murah?”\n"
"- “Apakah bepergian nanti lebih murah?”\n"
"- “Apakah kereta dengan transfer lebih murah?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada tiket diskon yang tersisa?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya naik kereta yang lebih lambat?”\n"
"\n"
"### Koneksi terlalu singkat\n"
"\n"
"Anda bisa bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah ada opsi dengan transfer yang lebih lama?”\n"
"- “Apa yang terjadi jika saya ketinggalan koneksi?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya menggunakan kereta berikutnya?”\n"
"- “Apakah tiket saya tetap berlaku?”\n"
"\n"
"### Rencana Anda mungkin berubah\n"
"\n"
"Tanyakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bisakah saya mengganti tiket ini nanti?”\n"
"- “Berapa biayanya untuk mengubahnya?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya menerima pengembalian uang?”\n"
"- “Apa yang terjadi jika saya ketinggalan kereta?”\n"
"- “Apakah tiket fleksibel tersedia?”\n"
"\n"
"### Kereta ditunda atau dibatalkan\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan berguna meliputi:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah kereta telah ditunda?”\n"
"- “Berapa lama penundaannya?”\n"
"- “Apakah kereta dibatalkan?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya menggunakan tiket ini pada kereta lain?”\n"
"- “Di mana saya bisa meminta pengembalian uang?”\n"
"- “Apakah saya akan melewatkan koneksi saya?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda membantu saya menemukan rute lain?”\n"
"\n"
"## Memahami Pengumuman Stasiun\n"
"\n"
"Di stasiun, Anda mungkin mendengar pengumuman seperti:\n"
"\n"
"- “Kereta telah ditunda.”\n"
"- “Peronnya telah berubah.”\n"
"- “Kereta sekarang berangkat dari peron delapan.”\n"
"- “Kereta telah dibatalkan.”\n"
"- “Kereta ini berhenti di sini.”\n"
"- “Tolong jangan naik kereta ini.”\n"
"- “Kereta siap untuk naik.”\n"
"- “Perhatikan jarak antara kereta dan peron.”\n"
"\n"
"Periksa papan keberangkatan secara teratur, karena nomor peron bisa berubah "
"sesaat sebelum keberangkatan.\n"
"\n"
"## Percakapan Pembelian Tiket Sederhana\n"
"\n"
"Percakapan tipikal mungkin terlihat seperti ini:\n"
"\n"
"> **Pelancong:** Halo, saya ingin tiket ke Kraków untuk besok pagi.  \n"
"> **Agen:** Tentu. Apakah Anda ingin tiket sekali jalan atau pulang-pergi?  "
"\n"
"> **Pelancong:** Tiket pulang-pergi, tolong. Saya ingin kembali pada Minggu "
"malam.  \n"
"> **Agen:** Ada kereta langsung besok pukul 9:15. Tiba pukul 11:50.  \n"
"> **Pelancong:** Apakah reservasi kursi termasuk?  \n"
"> **Agen:** Ya. Apakah Anda lebih suka kursi jendela atau lorong?  \n"
"> **Pelancong:** Kursi jendela, tolong. Berapa harga tiketnya?  \n"
"> **Agen:** Totalnya 160 złoty.  \n"
"> **Pelancong:** Apakah ada opsi yang lebih murah?  \n"
"> **Agen:** Ada kereta lain pukul 10:05 dengan satu transfer. Harganya 125 "
"złoty.  \n"
"> **Pelancong:** Berapa lama transfernya?  \n"
"> **Agen:** Dua puluh lima menit.  \n"
"> **Pelancong:** Itu terdengar baik. Saya akan mengambil opsi itu.\n"
"\n"
"## Formula Pembelian Tiket Sederhana\n"
"\n"
"Saat membeli tiket, ikuti struktur ini:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Tujuan:** Katakan ke mana Anda ingin pergi.\n"
"2. **Tanggal dan waktu:** Jelaskan kapan Anda ingin bepergian.\n"
"3. **Jenis tiket:** Pilih sekali jalan atau pulang-pergi.\n"
"4. **Rute:** Tanyakan apakah perjalanannya langsung.\n"
"5. **Kondisi:** Konfirmasi harga, fleksibilitas, dan reservasi kursi.\n"
"6. **Pemeriksaan akhir:** Ulangi waktu keberangkatan dan informasi peron.\n"
"7. **Pembayaran:** Pilih cara Anda ingin membayar.\n"
"\n"
"Misalnya:\n"
"\n"
"> “Saya ingin tiket pulang-pergi ke Wina untuk Jumat pagi, kembali pada "
"Minggu malam. Saya lebih suka kereta langsung dan kursi jendela.”\n"
"\n"
"## Skenario Latihan\n"
"\n"
"Dalam permainan peran ini, Anda membeli tiket kereta di Stasiun Pusat. Agen "
"tiket AI akan membantu Anda membandingkan keberangkatan, jenis tiket, rute, "
"dan harga.\n"
"\n"
"Selama percakapan, cobalah untuk:\n"
"\n"
"- Jelaskan tujuan dan waktu perjalanan yang Anda inginkan.\n"
"- Pilih antara tiket sekali jalan dan pulang-pergi.\n"
"- Tanyakan apakah perjalanannya langsung.\n"
"- Konfirmasi waktu keberangkatan dan kedatangan.\n"
"- Tanyakan tentang harga dan kondisi tiket.\n"
"- Meminta preferensi kursi.\n"
"- Merespons satu komplikasi, seperti kereta yang penuh, transfer, atau "
"harga yang lebih tinggi dari yang diharapkan.\n"
"- Konfirmasi detail perjalanan akhir sebelum membayar.\n"
"\n"
"Fokus pada mendapatkan informasi yang Anda butuhkan dan memastikan bahwa "
"Anda memahaminya dengan benar. Tata bahasa yang sempurna kurang penting "
"daripada memilih perjalanan dan tiket yang benar."

