#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/hotel-check-in.ts:13
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Checking into a hotel usually follows a predictable pattern. The "
"receptionist confirms your identity and reservation, explains the hotel’s "
"services, and gives you access to your room.\n"
"\n"
"Knowing a few key phrases can make the process much easier, especially when "
"you are travelling in a country where you do not speak the local language "
"confidently.\n"
"\n"
"## What You May Need at Check-In\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist may ask you for:\n"
"\n"
"- Your full name\n"
"- A passport or identity document\n"
"- Your booking confirmation\n"
"- A payment card\n"
"- The number of guests\n"
"- Your expected check-out date\n"
"\n"
"You can begin the conversation with:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hello, I have a reservation.”\n"
"- “Hi, I’d like to check in.”\n"
"- “The reservation should be under Alex Dmowski.”\n"
"- “I booked the room through a booking website.”\n"
"- “Here is my booking confirmation.”\n"
"\n"
"If the receptionist cannot find your reservation, stay calm and provide "
"more details:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you check the booking number?”\n"
"- “I received a confirmation email yesterday.”\n"
"- “The reservation may be under my partner’s name.”\n"
"- “Would it help if I showed you the confirmation?”\n"
"\n"
"## Confirm the Important Details\n"
"\n"
"Before accepting the room, confirm that the reservation details are "
"correct.\n"
"\n"
"You may want to check:\n"
"\n"
"- The room type\n"
"- The number of nights\n"
"- The total price\n"
"- Whether breakfast is included\n"
"- The number and size of beds\n"
"- The check-out time\n"
"- Any additional fees or deposits\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you confirm which room type I booked?”\n"
"- “Is breakfast included in the price?”\n"
"- “What time is check-out?”\n"
"- “Is there a security deposit?”\n"
"- “Are there any additional charges?”\n"
"- “Has the room already been paid for?”\n"
"- “Could I have a receipt, please?”\n"
"\n"
"Do not be afraid to ask the receptionist to repeat information:\n"
"\n"
"- “Sorry, could you repeat that?”\n"
"- “Could you speak a little more slowly, please?”\n"
"- “Did you say check-out is at eleven?”\n"
"- “Could you write that down for me?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Hotel Services\n"
"\n"
"Check-in is a good time to ask practical questions about your stay.\n"
"\n"
"### Wi-Fi\n"
"\n"
"- “Is Wi-Fi included?”\n"
"- “What is the Wi-Fi password?”\n"
"- “Does the Wi-Fi work inside the rooms?”\n"
"\n"
"### Breakfast\n"
"\n"
"- “What time is breakfast served?”\n"
"- “Where is the breakfast area?”\n"
"- “Do you have vegetarian options?”\n"
"- “Can I add breakfast to my reservation?”\n"
"\n"
"### Hotel facilities\n"
"\n"
"- “Does the hotel have a gym?”\n"
"- “Is there a place where I can leave my luggage?”\n"
"- “Do you have laundry service?”\n"
"- “Is room service available?”\n"
"- “Is there a restaurant in the hotel?”\n"
"\n"
"### Transport and local information\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you help me call a taxi?”\n"
"- “What is the easiest way to get to the city centre?”\n"
"- “Is there a bus stop nearby?”\n"
"- “Could you recommend a restaurant in the area?”\n"
"\n"
"## Make a Special Request\n"
"\n"
"It is best to make important requests before arriving, but you can also ask "
"at reception.\n"
"\n"
"Common requests include:\n"
"\n"
"- A quiet room\n"
"- A room on a higher or lower floor\n"
"- Two separate beds\n"
"- A larger bed\n"
"- A baby cot\n"
"- An accessible room\n"
"- Extra towels or pillows\n"
"- Early check-in\n"
"- Late check-out\n"
"- A room away from the lift\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases:\n"
"\n"
"- “Would it be possible to have a quiet room?”\n"
"- “Could I have a room away from the lift?”\n"
"- “Do you have a room on a higher floor?”\n"
"- “Could we have two separate beds?”\n"
"- “Would it be possible to check out later?”\n"
"- “Could you send an extra towel to the room?”\n"
"\n"
"Using “Could I…?”, “Would it be possible…?” and “Do you have…?” makes your "
"request sound polite and natural.\n"
"\n"
"## Handle Common Problems\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes the room is not ready, the booking details are incorrect, or the "
"room does not match what you reserved.\n"
"\n"
"### The room is not ready\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you know when the room will be ready?”\n"
"- “Could I leave my luggage here?”\n"
"- “Could you let me know when I can check in?”\n"
"- “Is there somewhere I can wait?”\n"
"\n"
"### The reservation cannot be found\n"
"\n"
"- “I have a confirmation email. Could you check it?”\n"
"- “Could you search using the booking reference?”\n"
"- “The reservation may be under a different name.”\n"
"- “Could you contact the booking platform?”\n"
"\n"
"### The room is different from the booking\n"
"\n"
"- “I believe I booked a double room.”\n"
"- “My confirmation says that breakfast is included.”\n"
"- “I requested two separate beds.”\n"
"- “Could you check the original reservation?”\n"
"- “Is another room available?”\n"
"\n"
"### There is a problem with the room\n"
"\n"
"- “The air conditioning does not seem to work.”\n"
"- “The room has not been cleaned yet.”\n"
"- “There is a lot of noise coming from the next room.”\n"
"- “The Wi-Fi is not working in my room.”\n"
"- “Could someone take a look at it?”\n"
"- “Would it be possible to change rooms?”\n"
"\n"
"Describe the problem clearly, explain what you expected, and ask for a "
"specific solution.\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Common Receptionist Questions\n"
"\n"
"A receptionist may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “May I have your name?”\n"
"- “Could I see your passport or ID?”\n"
"- “Do you have your booking confirmation?”\n"
"- “How many nights will you be staying?”\n"
"- “Will you be paying by card or cash?”\n"
"- “Would you like breakfast included?”\n"
"- “Do you need help with your luggage?”\n"
"- “Would you like a wake-up call?”\n"
"- “Do you have any special requests?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to give long answers. Clear and direct responses are "
"usually best.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “Yes, the reservation is under Dmowski. I’ll be staying for three nights, "
"and I’ll pay by card.”\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Check-In Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical conversation may follow this structure:\n"
"\n"
"1. Greet the receptionist.\n"
"2. Say that you have a reservation.\n"
"3. Give your name and identification.\n"
"4. Confirm your booking details.\n"
"5. Ask about breakfast, Wi-Fi, or check-out.\n"
"6. Make any special requests.\n"
"7. Collect your room key and directions.\n"
"8. Thank the receptionist.\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"> **Guest:** Hello, I have a reservation under Dmowski.  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Certainly. May I see your passport, please?  \n"
"> **Guest:** Of course. Here you are. Is breakfast included in my booking?  "
"\n"
"> **Receptionist:** Yes, it is served from seven until ten.  \n"
"> **Guest:** Great. Could you also tell me the Wi-Fi password?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** It is written on your key card.  \n"
"> **Guest:** Thank you. What time is check-out?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Check-out is at eleven.  \n"
"> **Guest:** Perfect. Thank you for your help.\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you have arrived at a hotel where you already have a "
"reservation. The AI receptionist will ask for your details, explain the "
"hotel’s services, and respond to your questions.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Introduce yourself and confirm your reservation.\n"
"- Ask at least two questions about the hotel.\n"
"- Make one polite request.\n"
"- Confirm an important detail by repeating it.\n"
"- Respond to an unexpected issue if one occurs.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on communicating clearly rather than using perfect grammar. A "
"successful check-in is one where both you and the receptionist understand "
"what needs to happen next."
msgstr ""
"Memeriksa masuk ke hotel biasanya mengikuti pola yang dapat diprediksi. "
"Resepsionis mengonfirmasi identitas dan reservasi Anda, menjelaskan layanan "
"hotel, dan memberi Anda akses ke kamar Anda.\n"
"\n"
"Mengetahui beberapa frasa kunci bisa membuat proses tersebut jauh lebih "
"mudah, terutama saat Anda bepergian ke negara di mana Anda tidak berbicara "
"bahasa setempat dengan percaya diri.\n"
"\n"
"## Apa yang Mungkin Anda Butuhkan saat Check-In\n"
"\n"
"Resepsionis mungkin meminta Anda untuk:\n"
"\n"
"- Nama lengkap Anda\n"
"- Paspor atau dokumen identitas\n"
"- Konfirmasi pemesanan Anda\n"
"- Kartu pembayaran\n"
"- Jumlah tamu\n"
"- Tanggal perkiraan check-out Anda\n"
"\n"
"Anda bisa memulai percakapan dengan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Halo, saya punya reservasi.”\n"
"- “Hai, saya ingin check in.”\n"
"- “Reservasi atas nama Alex Dmowski.”\n"
"- “Saya memesan kamar melalui situs pemesanan.”\n"
"- “Ini konfirmasi pemesanan saya.”\n"
"\n"
"Jika resepsionis tidak dapat menemukan reservasi Anda, tetap tenang dan "
"berikan lebih banyak detail:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda memeriksa nomor pemesanan?”\n"
"- “Saya menerima email konfirmasi kemarin.”\n"
"- “Reservasi mungkin atas nama pasangan saya.”\n"
"- “Apakah akan membantu jika saya menunjukkan konfirmasi?”\n"
"\n"
"## Konfirmasi Detail Penting\n"
"\n"
"Sebelum menerima kamar, pastikan bahwa detail reservasi sudah benar.\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin ingin memeriksa:\n"
"\n"
"- Jenis kamar\n"
"- Jumlah malam menginap\n"
"- Total harga\n"
"- Apakah sarapan sudah termasuk\n"
"- Jumlah dan ukuran tempat tidur\n"
"- Waktu check-out\n"
"- Biaya tambahan atau deposit\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan yang berguna meliputi:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda mengonfirmasi jenis kamar yang saya pesan?”\n"
"- “Apakah sarapan termasuk dalam harga?”\n"
"- “Jam berapa check-out?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada deposit keamanan?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada biaya tambahan?”\n"
"- “Apakah kamar sudah dibayar?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya mendapatkan kwitansi, tolong?\"\n"
"\n"
"Jangan takut untuk meminta resepsionis mengulangi informasi:\n"
"\n"
"- “Maaf, bisakah Anda mengulanginya?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda berbicara sedikit lebih lambat, tolong?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda mengatakan check-out jam sebelas?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda menuliskannya untuk saya?”\n"
"\n"
"## Tanyakan Tentang Layanan Hotel\n"
"\n"
"Check-in adalah waktu yang baik untuk menanyakan pertanyaan praktis tentang "
"masa menginap Anda.\n"
"\n"
"### Wi-Fi\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah Wi-Fi termasuk?”\n"
"- “Apa kata sandi Wi-Fi?”\n"
"- “Apakah Wi-Fi berfungsi di dalam kamar?”\n"
"\n"
"### Sarapan\n"
"\n"
"- “Jam berapa sarapan disajikan?”\n"
"- “Di mana area sarapan?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda memiliki pilihan vegetarian?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya menambahkan sarapan ke reservasi saya?”\n"
"\n"
"### Fasilitas Hotel\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah hotel memiliki gym?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada tempat untuk meninggalkan bagasi saya?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada layanan laundry?”\n"
"- “Apakah layanan kamar tersedia?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada restoran di hotel?”\n"
"\n"
"### Transport dan informasi lokal\n"
"\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda membantu saya memanggil taksi?”\n"
"- “Apa cara termudah untuk sampai ke pusat kota?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada halte bus di dekat sini?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda merekomendasikan restoran di area ini?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ajukan Permintaan Khusus\n"
"\n"
"Sebaiknya ajukan permintaan penting sebelum tiba, tetapi Anda juga bisa "
"bertanya di resepsi.\n"
"\n"
"Permintaan umum meliputi:\n"
"\n"
"- Kamar yang tenang\n"
"- Kamar di lantai yang lebih tinggi atau lebih rendah\n"
"- Dua tempat tidur terpisah\n"
"- Tempat tidur yang lebih besar\n"
"- Tempat tidur bayi\n"
"- Kamar yang dapat diakses\n"
"- Handuk atau bantal ekstra\n"
"- Check-in lebih awal\n"
"- Check-out lebih lambat\n"
"- Kamar jauh dari lift\n"
"\n"
"Frasa yang berguna:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah mungkin mendapatkan kamar yang tenang?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya mendapatkan kamar jauh dari lift?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda memiliki kamar di lantai yang lebih tinggi?”\n"
"- “Bisakah kami mendapatkan dua tempat tidur terpisah?”\n"
"- “Apakah mungkin untuk check-out lebih lambat?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda mengirimkan handuk ekstra ke kamar?”\n"
"\n"
"Menggunakan “Bisakah saya…?”, “Apakah mungkin…?” dan “Apakah Anda "
"memiliki…?” membuat permintaan Anda terdengar sopan dan alami.\n"
"\n"
"## Menangani Masalah Umum\n"
"\n"
"Terkadang kamar belum siap, detail pemesanan salah, atau kamar tidak sesuai "
"dengan yang Anda pesan.\n"
"\n"
"### Kamar tidak siap\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah Anda tahu kapan kamar akan siap?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya meninggalkan bagasi saya di sini?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda memberi tahu saya kapan saya bisa check in?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada tempat untuk menunggu?”\n"
"\n"
"### Reservasi tidak dapat ditemukan\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya punya email konfirmasi. Bisakah Anda memeriksanya?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda mencari menggunakan referensi pemesanan?”\n"
"- “Reservasi mungkin atas nama yang berbeda.”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda menghubungi platform pemesanan?”\n"
"\n"
"### Kamar berbeda dari pemesanan\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya percaya saya memesannya double room.”\n"
"- “Konfirmasi saya mengatakan bahwa sarapan termasuk.”\n"
"- “Saya meminta dua tempat tidur terpisah.”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda memeriksa reservasi asli?”\n"
"- “Apakah kamar lain tersedia?”\n"
"\n"
"### Ada masalah dengan kamar\n"
"\n"
"- “AC sepertinya tidak berfungsi.”\n"
"- “Kamar belum dibersihkan.”\n"
"- “Ada banyak suara dari kamar sebelah.”\n"
"- “Wi-Fi tidak berfungsi di kamar saya.”\n"
"- “Bisakah seseorang memeriksanya?”\n"
"- “Apakah mungkin untuk mengganti kamar?”\n"
"\n"
"Jelaskan masalah dengan jelas, jelaskan apa yang Anda harapkan, dan minta "
"solusi tertentu.\n"
"\n"
"## Pahami Pertanyaan Resepsionis yang Umum\n"
"\n"
"Resepsionis mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mengetahui nama Anda?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya melihat paspor atau ID Anda?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda memiliki konfirmasi pemesanan Anda?”\n"
"- “Berapa malam Anda akan menginap?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda akan membayar dengan kartu atau uang tunai?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda ingin sarapan termasuk?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda membutuhkan bantuan dengan bagasi Anda?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda ingin panggilan bangun?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda memiliki permintaan khusus?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak perlu memberikan jawaban panjang. Respons yang jelas dan "
"langsung biasanya yang terbaik.\n"
"\n"
"Sebagai contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> “Ya, reservasinya atas nama Dmowski. Saya akan menginap selama tiga "
"malam, dan saya akan membayar dengan kartu.”\n"
"\n"
"## Percakapan Check-In yang Sederhana\n"
"\n"
"Percakapan khas mungkin mengikuti struktur ini:\n"
"\n"
"1. Sambut resepsionis.\n"
"2. Katakan bahwa Anda memiliki reservasi.\n"
"3. Beri nama dan identifikasi Anda.\n"
"4. Konfirmasikan detail pemesanan Anda.\n"
"5. Tanyakan tentang sarapan, Wi-Fi, atau check-out.\n"
"6. Buat permintaan khusus.\n"
"7. Ambil kunci kamar dan petunjuk.\n"
"8. Ucapkan terima kasih kepada resepsionis.\n"
"\n"
"Contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> **Tamu:** Halo, saya punya reservasi atas nama Dmowski.  \n"
"> **Resepsionis:** Tentu. Bolehkah saya melihat paspor Anda, tolong?  \n"
"> **Tamu:** Tentu. Ini dia. Apakah sarapan termasuk dalam pemesanan saya?  \n"
"> **Resepsionis:** Ya, disajikan dari jam tujuh sampai sepuluh.  \n"
"> **Tamu:** Baik. Bisakah Anda juga memberi tahu saya kata sandi Wi-Fi?  \n"
"> **Resepsionis:** Itu tertulis di kartu kunci Anda.  \n"
"> **Tamu:** Terima kasih. Jam berapa check-out?  \n"
"> **Resepsionis:** Check-out jam sebelas.  \n"
"> **Tamu:** Sempurna. Terima kasih atas bantuan Anda.\n"
"\n"
"## Skenario Latihan\n"
"\n"
"Dalam permainan peran ini, Anda telah tiba di hotel di mana Anda sudah "
"memiliki reservasi. Resepsionis AI akan meminta detail Anda, menjelaskan "
"layanan hotel, dan menjawab pertanyaan Anda.\n"
"\n"
"Selama percakapan, cobalah untuk:\n"
"\n"
"- Memperkenalkan diri dan konfirmasikan reservasi Anda.\n"
"- Ajukan setidaknya dua pertanyaan tentang hotel.\n"
"- Buat satu permintaan sopan.\n"
"- Konfirmasikan detail penting dengan mengulanginya.\n"
"- Tanggapi masalah yang tidak terduga jika terjadi.\n"
"\n"
"Fokus pada komunikasi yang jelas daripada menggunakan tata bahasa yang "
"sempurna. Check-in yang sukses adalah ketika Anda dan resepsionis memahami "
"apa yang perlu dilakukan selanjutnya."

