#: src/features/Blog/blogData.tsx:133
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"I am not a talented software developer. I'm not the fastest one — and "
"definitely not the best. But when the company where I work struggles with "
"something important and urgent, they ask for my help and pay me a lot. No "
"clue why.\n"
"\n"
"The company makes chatbots for entertainment. You know those ads like "
"*“Let’s talk with Albert Einstein”* or *“Let’s chat with Marilyn Monroe.”* "
"Which I find quite stupid — but it works. Well, it had been working, to be "
"precise. The company got stuck. No ideas for new features, no interesting "
"characters. Whoever wanted to try it already had. Revenue slowly declined. "
"The team’s writer, who was hired to craft such personas, couldn’t keep up, "
"and quality was slipping.\n"
"\n"
"Our task was to improve it — with no real idea how. That’s all you need to "
"know about my employer’s management and processes, or lack of processes, "
"vision, plan, responsibilities. But okay.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/monroe.webp)\n"
"\n"
"The writer's idea was to create a famous person who had tried another life "
"— so the user could talk, for example, with Donald Trump, who in the middle "
"of his life decided to switch careers and become a painter. Maybe our "
"writer got inspired by Donald’s recently announced drawing, allegedly sent "
"to Epstein. But anyway. The writer gave me a one-page draft about Donald's "
"life after his career pivot.\n"
"\n"
"Which was not enough to create a good AI persona. I needed at least 20 "
"pages of text to fill our QDrant vector store, so the AI RAG system could "
"freely pick well-embedded documents for a proper fine-tuning process. "
"*Sorry for the engineering terms.*\n"
"\n"
"After one day of waiting, I decided to use AI to generate what our writer "
"might have written. It was an act of procrastination. I just wanted to fill "
"the waiting time. Surprisingly, the results were almost identical to what "
"the writer gave me. That, to be honest, astonished me.\n"
"\n"
"It might have been a coincidence, so I wanted to re-check it with real data "
"— with my personal data. Later, I realized that was the wrong decision.\n"
"\n"
"The company was in a rush. *“We needed this persona done yesterday,”* said "
"the founder. I was skeptical that this persona would rejuvenate the "
"company. I asked for two extra days to finish my work. Most of the time I "
"planned to allocate to my experiments.\n"
"\n"
"After collecting all my personal data — including Telegram chats, voice "
"call transcripts, Google Photos, Google Drive documents, everything somehow "
"related to me — I stared at the progress bar with a kind smile. My dog "
"barked in the background, demanding attention. I ignored him, eyes fixed on "
"the screen.\n"
"\n"
"The kind smile disappeared when I got the extrapolation result.\n"
"\n"
"> “You, Alex, will be fired tomorrow,” the screen read.\n"
"\n"
"That had to be wrong. I repeat, I’m not a talented developer and not the "
"best one — but when the company struggles with something, they ask for my "
"help. I did a lot for them. I’m important to them. It was ridiculous.\n"
"\n"
"Ridiculous or not, that day I finished my task and sent the results "
"immediately after. The rest of the day I spent in my apartment in a "
"beautiful neighborhood somewhere in Warsaw — with a slightly greenish face.\n"
"\n"
"*\"This is ridiculous,\"* I kept hearing in my head.\n"
"\n"
"*“Listen, Alex, I like you…”* — that’s how my manager started the "
"conversation the next day.\n"
"\n"
"He listed what I had done for them, what the company was doing, that they "
"had to reduce spending, that they really appreciated my work — and many "
"other bullshit epithets.\n"
"\n"
"*“So we've decided to pause your working relationship for a while and focus "
"on company survival.”* — that’s how he finished.\n"
"\n"
"That was not funny at all. It took me three days to accept it. At least I "
"had good savings — and that creepy piece of software.\n"
"\n"
"After three days of staring at the ceiling, I came back to the software. "
"What else could I do? I was unemployed, emotionally bruised, and curious.\n"
"\n"
"I opened the extrapolation interface and typed:\n"
"\n"
"> “What if we didn’t get a dog one year ago?”\n"
"\n"
"Result: In 99.9% of variations — we still got a dog. Just later.  \n"
"Sometimes it’s a whippet. Sometimes it’s a mutt. In one rare case, we got a "
"cat. The cat ran away in six months.\n"
"\n"
"Next test:  \n"
"\n"
"> “What if I won the lottery?”\n"
"\n"
"Great news — I did. Once or twice in different timelines. And then I lost "
"it all on real estate in Italy or shady crypto startups. No happiness was "
"detected.\n"
"\n"
"And then I grew bolder.\n"
"\n"
"I asked the real question — the one I had always wanted to know the answer "
"to:\n"
"\n"
"> “What if I won the programming olympiads 15 years ago?”\n"
"\n"
"Result: life shift. Massive.\n"
"\n"
"That version of me entered a top university in another country. He made "
"friends — actual friends, with opinions and a taste in architecture. He "
"co-founded a machine learning startup before I even learned how to hold eye "
"contact in interviews.\n"
"\n"
"And weirdest of all — he seemed… happy?\n"
"\n"
"I scrolled through his life logs. He drank smoothies in Palo Alto. He "
"surfed. He pitched to venture capitalists and got rejected. Then he pitched "
"again. Eventually, he failed gracefully.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/polo.webp)\n"
"\n"
"He dated people I couldn't even imagine existing. He read poetry. He even "
"had a therapist.\n"
"\n"
"But the strangest part? Near the end of his timeline, he left a private "
"note in the system:\n"
"\n"
"> “Sometimes I wonder what my life would’ve been like if I stayed in "
"Poland. Maybe in a small apartment in Warsaw. Maybe walking a dog. I think "
"I’d like that too.”\n"
"\n"
"That’s when I closed the laptop.\n"
"\n"
"I didn’t touch the software for a week. I went on long walks. Listened to "
"music without skipping every 30 seconds.\n"
"\n"
"All the timelines, all the versions of me, all the simulations — they "
"echoed in my head like reruns of a show I’d already watched.\n"
"\n"
"I realized that the drastic changes made me unrecognizable. They weren’t me "
"— just projections. Branches growing in every direction, but from a root I "
"barely remembered planting.\n"
"\n"
"I opened the app one last time.  \n"
"Final prompt:  \n"
"\n"
"> “What if I don’t ask anymore?”\n"
"\n"
"The system froze. Then replied:  \n"
"\n"
"> “No projections available.”\n"
"\n"
"Good.\n"
"\n"
"I shut the laptop down and archived the logs.\n"
"\n"
"The dog stared at me. He usually does that when it’s time for a walk — at 3 "
"p.m.\n"
"\n"
"And for the first time in weeks, I didn’t want to be anywhere else.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/dog-park2.webp)\n"
msgstr ""
"Saya bukan pengembang perangkat lunak yang berbakat. Saya bukan yang "
"tercepat — dan tentu saja bukan yang terbaik. Tetapi ketika perusahaan "
"tempat saya bekerja mengalami kesulitan dengan sesuatu yang penting dan "
"mendesak, mereka meminta bantuan saya dan membayar saya banyak. Tidak tahu "
"kenapa.\n"
"\n"
"Perusahaan ini membuat chatbot untuk hiburan. Anda tahu iklan seperti *“Ayo "
"bicara dengan Albert Einstein”* atau *“Ayo ngobrol dengan Marilyn Monroe.”* "
"Yang menurut saya cukup konyol — tetapi berhasil. Ya, lebih tepatnya dulu "
"berhasil. Perusahaan mengalami kebuntuan. Tidak ada ide untuk fitur baru, "
"tidak ada karakter menarik. Siapa pun yang ingin mencobanya sudah "
"melakukannya. Pendapatan perlahan menurun. Penulis tim, yang dipekerjakan "
"untuk membuat persona semacam itu, tidak dapat mengejar, dan kualitasnya "
"menurun.\n"
"\n"
"Tugas kami adalah memperbaikinya — tanpa ide nyata bagaimana caranya. Itu "
"saja yang perlu Anda ketahui tentang manajemen dan proses (atau kekurangan "
"proses, visi, rencana, tanggung jawab) dari perusahaan saya. Tapi baiklah.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/monroe.webp)\n"
"\n"
"Ide penulisnya adalah menciptakan orang terkenal yang mencoba kehidupan "
"lain — jadi pengguna bisa berbicara, misalnya, dengan Donald Trump, yang di "
"tengah hidupnya memutuskan beralih karier dan menjadi pelukis. Mungkin "
"penulis kami terinspirasi oleh pengumuman menggambar Donald yang baru-baru "
"ini, yang diduga dikirim ke Epstein. Tapi bagaimanapun juga. Penulis "
"memberikan draf satu halaman kepada saya tentang kehidupan Donald setelah "
"perubahan kariernya.\n"
"\n"
"Yang belum cukup untuk menciptakan persona AI yang baik. Saya memerlukan "
"setidaknya 20 halaman teks untuk mengisi QDrant vector store kami, sehingga "
"sistem AI RAG dapat dengan bebas memilih dokumen yang tertanam dengan baik "
"untuk proses penyetelan ulang yang tepat. *Maaf untuk istilah teknisnya.*\n"
"\n"
"Setelah menunggu satu hari, saya memutuskan untuk menggunakan AI untuk "
"menghasilkan apa yang mungkin telah ditulis oleh penulis kami. Itu adalah "
"tindakan menunda-nunda pekerjaan. Saya hanya ingin mengisi waktu menunggu. "
"Yang mengejutkan, hasilnya hampir identik dengan yang diberikan penulis "
"kepada saya. Itu, sejujurnya, membuat saya terkejut.\n"
"\n"
"Mungkin itu kebetulan, jadi saya ingin memeriksanya kembali dengan data "
"nyata — dengan data pribadi saya. Belakangan, saya menyadari bahwa itu "
"adalah keputusan yang salah.\n"
"\n"
"Perusahaan sedang terburu-buru. *“Kami butuh persona ini selesai kemarin,”* "
"kata pendiri. Saya ragu bahwa persona ini akan menyegarkan perusahaan. Saya "
"meminta dua hari ekstra untuk menyelesaikan pekerjaan saya. Sebagian besar "
"waktu saya rencanakan untuk dialokasikan ke eksperimen saya.\n"
"\n"
"Setelah mengumpulkan semua data pribadi saya — termasuk percakapan "
"Telegram, transkrip panggilan suara, foto Google, dokumen Google Drive, "
"semua yang entah bagaimana terkait dengan saya — saya menatap bilah "
"kemajuan dengan senyum ramah. Anjing saya menggonggong di latar belakang, "
"menuntut perhatian. Saya mengabaikannya, mata menatap layar.\n"
"\n"
"Senyum ramah menghilang ketika saya mendapatkan hasil ekstrapolasi.\n"
"\n"
"> \"Kamu, Alex, akan dipecat besok,\" tertulis di layar.\n"
"\n"
"Itu pasti salah. Saya ulangi, saya bukan pengembang yang berbakat dan bukan "
"yang terbaik — tetapi ketika perusahaan mengalami kesulitan dengan sesuatu, "
"mereka meminta bantuan saya. Saya telah melakukan banyak hal untuk mereka. "
"Saya penting bagi mereka. Itu sangat tidak masuk akal.\n"
"\n"
"Tidak masuk akal atau tidak, hari itu saya menyelesaikan tugas saya dan "
"mengirimkan hasilnya segera setelahnya. Sisa hari itu saya habiskan di "
"apartemen saya di lingkungan yang indah di suatu tempat di Warsawa — dengan "
"wajah yang sedikit kehijauan.\n"
"\n"
"*“Ini tidak masuk akal,\"* terus berulang di kepala saya.\n"
"\n"
"*“Dengar, Alex, aku suka kamu…”* — begitulah manajer saya memulai "
"percakapan keesokan harinya.\n"
"\n"
"Dia mencantumkan apa yang telah saya lakukan untuk mereka, apa yang "
"dilakukan perusahaan, bahwa mereka harus mengurangi pengeluaran, bahwa "
"mereka benar-benar menghargai pekerjaan saya — dan banyak epitet omong "
"kosong lainnya.\n"
"\n"
"*“Jadi kami telah memutuskan untuk menghentikan hubungan kerja Anda untuk "
"sementara waktu dan fokus pada kelangsungan perusahaan.”* — begitulah cara "
"dia menyelesaikan.\n"
"\n"
"Itu tidak lucu sama sekali. Saya butuh tiga hari untuk menerimanya. "
"Setidaknya saya punya tabungan yang bagus — dan perangkat lunak yang "
"menyeramkan itu.\n"
"\n"
"Setelah tiga hari menatap langit-langit, saya kembali ke perangkat lunak "
"itu. Apalagi yang bisa saya lakukan? Saya menganggur, terluka secara "
"emosional, dan penasaran.\n"
"\n"
"Saya membuka antarmuka ekstrapolasi dan mengetik:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Bagaimana jika kita tidak memelihara anjing satu tahun yang lalu?\"\n"
"\n"
"Hasil: Dalam 99,9% variasi — kita tetap mendapatkan anjing. Hanya "
"terlambat.  \n"
"Kadang-kadang itu adalah whippet. Kadang-kadang itu adalah anjing campuran. "
"Dalam satu kasus langka, kita mendapatkan kucing. Kucing itu kabur dalam "
"enam bulan.\n"
"\n"
"Tes berikutnya:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Bagaimana jika saya memenangkan lotere?\"\n"
"\n"
"Berita baik — saya menang. Satu atau dua kali di berbagai garis waktu. Dan "
"kemudian saya kehilangan semuanya pada properti di Italia atau startup "
"kripto yang samar. Tidak ada kebahagiaan yang terdeteksi.\n"
"\n"
"Dan kemudian saya semakin berani.\n"
"\n"
"Saya mengajukan pertanyaan sebenarnya — yang selalu ingin saya ketahui "
"jawabannya:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Bagaimana jika saya memenangkan olimpiade pemrograman 15 tahun yang "
"lalu?\"\n"
"\n"
"Hasil: perubahan hidup. Masif.\n"
"\n"
"Versi diri saya itu masuk ke universitas top di negara lain. Dia berteman — "
"teman sejati, dengan pendapat dan selera dalam arsitektur. Dia ikut "
"mendirikan startup pembelajaran mesin sebelum saya bahkan belajar cara "
"menjaga kontak mata dalam wawancara.\n"
"\n"
"Dan yang paling aneh — dia tampak… bahagia?\n"
"\n"
"Saya menggulir log kehidupannya. Dia meminum smoothie di Palo Alto. Dia "
"berselancar. Dia mempresentasikan ide kepada pemodal ventura dan ditolak. "
"Kemudian dia mencoba lagi. Akhirnya, dia gagal dengan anggun.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/polo.webp)\n"
"\n"
"Dia berkencan dengan orang yang bahkan tidak bisa saya bayangkan ada. Dia "
"membaca puisi. Dia bahkan memiliki terapis.\n"
"\n"
"Tetapi bagian yang paling aneh? Menjelang akhir garis waktunya, dia "
"meninggalkan catatan pribadi dalam sistem:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Terkadang saya bertanya-tanya bagaimana hidup saya akan berjalan kalau "
"tetap tinggal di Polandia. Mungkin tinggal di apartemen kecil di Warsawa. "
"Mungkin berjalan-jalan dengan anjing. Saya pikir saya akan menyukainya "
"juga.\"\n"
"\n"
"Saat itulah saya menutup laptop.\n"
"\n"
"Saya tidak menyentuh perangkat lunak selama seminggu. Saya berjalan-jalan "
"jauh. Mendengarkan musik tanpa melewatkan setiap 30 detik.\n"
"\n"
"Semua garis waktu, semua versi diriku, semua simulasi — mereka bergema di "
"kepala seperti tayangan ulang acara yang sudah pernah saya tonton.\n"
"\n"
"Saya menyadari bahwa perubahan drastis membuat saya tak bisa dikenali. "
"Mereka bukan saya — hanya proyeksi. Cabang tumbuh ke segala arah, tetapi "
"dari akar yang hampir tidak saya ingat menanamnya.\n"
"\n"
"Saya membuka aplikasi untuk terakhir kalinya.  \n"
"Prompt akhir:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Bagaimana jika saya tidak bertanya lagi?\"\n"
"\n"
"Sistem membeku. Kemudian menjawab:  \n"
"\n"
"> \"Tidak ada proyeksi yang tersedia.\"\n"
"\n"
"Bagus.\n"
"\n"
"Saya mematikan laptop dan mengarsipkan log.\n"
"\n"
"Anjing itu menatap saya. Dia biasa melakukannya saat sudah waktunya "
"berjalan-jalan — jam 3 sore.\n"
"\n"
"Dan untuk pertama kalinya dalam beberapa minggu, saya tidak ingin berada di "
"tempat lain.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/dog-park2.webp)"

