#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/at-the-grocery-store.ts:354
#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/returning-an-item-in-a-store.ts:22
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "Shopping"
msgstr "Belanja"

#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/at-the-grocery-store.ts:16
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Shopping at a grocery store involves many short but useful conversations. "
"You may need to find a product, ask about a price, understand a promotion, "
"check ingredients, or speak with a cashier.\n"
"\n"
"You do not need long or complicated sentences. Clear questions and polite "
"phrases are usually enough.\n"
"\n"
"## How to Ask Where Something Is\n"
"\n"
"When you cannot find a product, you can approach an employee and say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Excuse me, could you help me?”\n"
"- “Where can I find the milk?”\n"
"- “Which aisle is the pasta in?”\n"
"- “Do you know where the rice is?”\n"
"- “I’m looking for olive oil.”\n"
"- “Could you show me where it is?”\n"
"\n"
"An employee may respond with directions such as:\n"
"\n"
"- “It’s in aisle five.”\n"
"- “It’s next to the bread.”\n"
"- “You’ll find it at the back of the store.”\n"
"- “It’s on the top shelf.”\n"
"- “It’s in the refrigerated section.”\n"
"- “Follow me. I’ll show you.”\n"
"\n"
"Useful location words include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Aisle** — a passage between shelves\n"
"- **Shelf** — the surface where products are displayed\n"
"- **Checkout** — the place where you pay\n"
"- **Refrigerated section** — the area for chilled products\n"
"- **Frozen-food section** — the area containing frozen products\n"
"- **Produce section** — the area containing fruit and vegetables\n"
"- **Bakery section** — the area containing bread and baked goods\n"
"\n"
"## Ask Whether a Product Is Available\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes a shelf is empty or the product you need is difficult to find.\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you have this product?”\n"
"- “Do you sell oat milk?”\n"
"- “Is this item still available?”\n"
"- “Do you have any more in stock?”\n"
"- “When will this be available again?”\n"
"- “Is there another brand you would recommend?”\n"
"- “Do you have a similar product?”\n"
"\n"
"If the product is unavailable, an employee may say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m afraid it’s out of stock.”\n"
"- “We should have more tomorrow.”\n"
"- “That product has been discontinued.”\n"
"- “We have a similar one from another brand.”\n"
"- “Let me check in the storage room.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Prices\n"
"\n"
"Price labels can sometimes be unclear, especially when several products are "
"displayed together.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much is this?”\n"
"- “Could you check the price for me?”\n"
"- “Is this the correct price?”\n"
"- “Is the price per item or per kilogram?”\n"
"- “Does this include tax?”\n"
"- “Why is the price different at the checkout?”\n"
"- “Which one is cheaper?”\n"
"\n"
"You may also hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “It costs three ninety-nine.”\n"
"- “It’s sold by weight.”\n"
"- “The price is per kilogram.”\n"
"- “The discount is applied at the checkout.”\n"
"- “You need a loyalty card to get that price.”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Promotions and Discounts\n"
"\n"
"Stores often use promotional language that may be confusing.\n"
"\n"
"Common offers include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Buy one, get one free**\n"
"- **Two for five**\n"
"- **Twenty percent off**\n"
"- **Reduced price**\n"
"- **Special offer**\n"
"- **Member price**\n"
"- **Loyalty-card price**\n"
"- **Clearance**\n"
"- **Valid until Friday**\n"
"\n"
"Questions you can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is this product on sale?”\n"
"- “How does this promotion work?”\n"
"- “Do I need to buy two?”\n"
"- “Do I need a loyalty card?”\n"
"- “Is the discount applied automatically?”\n"
"- “When does the promotion end?”\n"
"- “Can I combine this offer with another discount?”\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “The label says two for five. Can I buy only one?”\n"
"\n"
"The employee may explain:\n"
"\n"
"> “Yes, but one item will cost three.”\n"
"\n"
"## Compare Products\n"
"\n"
"You may want to compare brands, sizes, ingredients, or prices.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “What is the difference between these two?”\n"
"- “Which one is more popular?”\n"
"- “Which one is better value?”\n"
"- “Is there a cheaper option?”\n"
"- “Do you have a larger size?”\n"
"- “Does this come in a smaller package?”\n"
"- “Which brand would you recommend?”\n"
"- “Is there a store-brand version?”\n"
"\n"
"A useful phrase is:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’m looking for something similar, but less expensive.”\n"
"\n"
"You can also explain your priorities:\n"
"\n"
"- “I need something without added sugar.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for a high-protein option.”\n"
"- “I’d prefer something organic.”\n"
"- “I need a product that will last several days.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for the best value, not necessarily the cheapest product.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Ingredients and Dietary Needs\n"
"\n"
"Checking ingredients is especially important if you have allergies or "
"dietary preferences.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Does this contain nuts?”\n"
"- “Is this gluten-free?”\n"
"- “Is this suitable for vegetarians?”\n"
"- “Is this vegan?”\n"
"- “Does this contain dairy?”\n"
"- “Is there any added sugar?”\n"
"- “Where can I find lactose-free products?”\n"
"- “Do you have a dairy-free alternative?”\n"
"\n"
"You can also say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m allergic to peanuts.”\n"
"- “I cannot eat gluten.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for something without dairy.”\n"
"- “Could you help me check the ingredients?”\n"
"\n"
"For serious allergies, always read the package carefully. A store employee "
"may help you find information, but they may not be able to guarantee that a "
"product is completely allergen-free.\n"
"\n"
"## Buy Fruit, Vegetables, Meat, or Cheese\n"
"\n"
"Some products are sold by weight rather than by package.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’d like one kilogram of apples, please.”\n"
"- “Could I have half a kilogram of tomatoes?”\n"
"- “I’d like three hundred grams of cheese.”\n"
"- “Could you give me six slices?”\n"
"- “Can I have two chicken breasts?”\n"
"- “That’s enough, thank you.”\n"
"\n"
"The employee may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much would you like?”\n"
"- “Is this amount okay?”\n"
"- “Would you like it sliced?”\n"
"- “Would you like anything else?”\n"
"- “Do you need a bag?”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “A little more, please.”\n"
"- “A little less, please.”\n"
"- “That amount is perfect.”\n"
"- “Could you slice it thinly?”\n"
"- “No, that’s everything.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Product Freshness\n"
"\n"
"You may want to check whether food is fresh or how long it will last.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “When does this expire?”\n"
"- “What is the use-by date?”\n"
"- “Was this baked today?”\n"
"- “Is this fresh?”\n"
"- “How long will this keep?”\n"
"- “Should I store this in the refrigerator?”\n"
"- “Can this be frozen?”\n"
"\n"
"Common date labels include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Best before** — the product may lose quality after this date\n"
"- **Use by** — the product should normally be consumed before this date\n"
"- **Packed on** — the date the product was packaged\n"
"- **Sell by** — a date mainly used by the store\n"
"\n"
"## Handle Problems with a Product\n"
"\n"
"You may notice that an item is damaged, open, expired, or incorrectly "
"labelled.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “This package is damaged.”\n"
"- “This bottle is leaking.”\n"
"- “I think this product has expired.”\n"
"- “The seal is broken.”\n"
"- “This item was on the wrong shelf.”\n"
"- “Could I exchange this for another one?”\n"
"- “Could someone check this product?”\n"
"\n"
"Stay polite and explain the problem clearly.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “Excuse me, this carton is leaking. Could I replace it?”\n"
"\n"
"## Speak at the Checkout\n"
"\n"
"When you reach the checkout, the cashier may ask several common questions:\n"
"\n"
"- “Did you find everything you needed?”\n"
"- “Do you have a loyalty card?”\n"
"- “Would you like a bag?”\n"
"- “Do you need a receipt?”\n"
"- “Are you paying by cash or card?”\n"
"- “Would you like to donate to charity?”\n"
"- “Do you need help packing?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful answers include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Yes, I found everything, thank you.”\n"
"- “No, I couldn’t find one item.”\n"
"- “I don’t have a loyalty card.”\n"
"- “Yes, one bag, please.”\n"
"- “No bag, thank you.”\n"
"- “I’ll pay by card.”\n"
"- “Could I have the receipt, please?”\n"
"- “Could I pay separately for these items?”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Checkout Instructions\n"
"\n"
"When paying by card, you may hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “Please insert your card.”\n"
"- “You can tap your card.”\n"
"- “Please enter your PIN.”\n"
"- “Your payment was declined.”\n"
"- “Would you like to try again?”\n"
"- “Please remove your card.”\n"
"- “The payment has gone through.”\n"
"\n"
"If something goes wrong, you can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could I try another card?”\n"
"- “Can I pay in cash instead?”\n"
"- “I think I was charged twice.”\n"
"- “Could you check the total?”\n"
"- “The price on the shelf was different.”\n"
"- “Could you remove this item, please?”\n"
"\n"
"## Use Self-Checkout\n"
"\n"
"At a self-checkout, you may need to ask an employee for help.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you help me with the self-checkout?”\n"
"- “The machine is not scanning this item.”\n"
"- “It says there is an unexpected item.”\n"
"- “How do I weigh the vegetables?”\n"
"- “Where do I enter the product number?”\n"
"- “How can I remove an item?”\n"
"- “The machine has not printed my receipt.”\n"
"\n"
"You may see or hear instructions such as:\n"
"\n"
"- “Scan your first item.”\n"
"- “Place the item in the bagging area.”\n"
"- “Select your payment method.”\n"
"- “Approval needed.”\n"
"- “Please wait for assistance.”\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Grocery Store Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical interaction may look like this:\n"
"\n"
"> **Customer:** Excuse me, could you help me find oat milk?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Of course. It’s in aisle six, next to the regular milk.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Thank you. Do you have an unsweetened version?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Yes, we have two brands. This one is currently on sale.  \n"
"> **Customer:** How does the promotion work?  \n"
"> **Employee:** It’s twenty percent off if you have a loyalty card.  \n"
"> **Customer:** I don’t have one. Is there a cheaper alternative?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Yes, the store-brand version is less expensive.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Great. Could you show me where it is?\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Shopping Formula\n"
"\n"
"When you need help, use this structure:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Get attention:** “Excuse me, could you help me?”\n"
"2. **Explain what you need:** “I’m looking for brown rice.”\n"
"3. **Ask a specific question:** “Which aisle is it in?”\n"
"4. **Clarify the answer:** “Did you say aisle seven?”\n"
"5. **Thank the employee:** “Great, thank you for your help.”\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are shopping at FreshMart. The AI employee will help "
"you find products, explain prices and promotions, and answer questions "
"about the store.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Ask where at least one product is located.\n"
"- Ask about a price or promotion.\n"
"- Compare two products.\n"
"- Ask about an ingredient or dietary requirement.\n"
"- Respond to one small problem, such as an unavailable product or unclear "
"price.\n"
"- Complete the purchase or end the interaction politely.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on communicating your needs clearly. You do not need perfect grammar "
"to have a successful conversation in a grocery store."
msgstr ""
"Berbelanja di toko bahan makanan melibatkan banyak percakapan singkat namun "
"berguna. Anda mungkin perlu menemukan sebuah produk, bertanya tentang "
"harga, memahami promosi, memeriksa bahan, atau berbicara dengan kasir.\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak perlu kalimat yang panjang atau rumit. Pertanyaan yang jelas dan "
"frasa sopan biasanya sudah cukup.\n"
"\n"
"## Cara Bertanya Di Mana Sesuatu Berada\n"
"\n"
"Ketika Anda tidak dapat menemukan sebuah produk, Anda dapat mendekati "
"seorang pegawai dan mengatakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Permisi, bisakah Anda membantu saya?”\n"
"- “Di mana saya bisa menemukan susu?”\n"
"- “Di lorong mana pasta itu berada?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda tahu di mana beras itu berada?”\n"
"- “Saya mencari minyak zaitun.”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda menunjukkan di mana letaknya?”\n"
"\n"
"Seorang pegawai mungkin merespon dengan petunjuk seperti:\n"
"\n"
"- “Itu ada di lorong lima.”\n"
"- “Itu ada di sebelah roti.”\n"
"- “Anda akan menemukannya di bagian belakang toko.”\n"
"- “Itu ada di rak paling atas.”\n"
"- “Itu ada di bagian pendingin.”\n"
"- “Ikuti saya. Saya akan menunjukkan.”\n"
"\n"
"Kata-kata lokasi yang berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- **Lorong** — jalan di antara rak\n"
"- **Rak** — permukaan tempat produk dipajang\n"
"- **Kasir** — tempat di mana Anda membayar\n"
"- **Bagian pendingin** — area untuk produk dingin\n"
"- **Bagian makanan beku** — area yang berisi produk beku\n"
"- **Bagian produk segar** — area yang berisi buah dan sayuran\n"
"- **Bagian roti** — area yang berisi roti dan makanan yang dipanggang\n"
"\n"
"## Tanya Apakah Sebuah Produk Tersedia\n"
"\n"
"Terkadang sebuah rak kosong atau produk yang Anda butuhkan sulit ditemukan.\n"
"\n"
"Anda bisa bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah Anda memiliki produk ini?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda menjual susu oat?”\n"
"- “Apakah item ini masih tersedia?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda punya stok lebih?”\n"
"- “Kapan ini akan tersedia lagi?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda merekomendasikan merek lain?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda memiliki produk serupa?”\n"
"\n"
"Jika produk tidak tersedia, pegawai bisa mengatakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Maaf, itu habis stok.”\n"
"- “Kita seharusnya memiliki lebih banyak besok.”\n"
"- “Produk itu sudah dihentikan.”\n"
"- “Kami memiliki yang serupa dari merek lain.”\n"
"- “Izinkan saya memeriksa di ruang penyimpanan.”\n"
"\n"
"## Tanya Tentang Harga\n"
"\n"
"Label harga terkadang bisa tidak jelas, terutama ketika beberapa produk "
"dipajang bersama.\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan yang berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Berapa harga ini?”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda memeriksa harganya untuk saya?”\n"
"- “Apakah ini harga yang benar?”\n"
"- “Apakah harga ini per item atau per kilogram?”\n"
"- “Apakah ini sudah termasuk pajak?”\n"
"- “Mengapa harga berbeda pada kasir?”\n"
"- “Yang mana yang lebih murah?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin juga mendengar:\n"
"\n"
"- “Harganya tiga sembilan puluh sembilan.”\n"
"- “Ini dijual per berat.”\n"
"- “Harganya per kilogram.”\n"
"- “Diskon diterapkan di kasir.”\n"
"- “Anda memerlukan kartu loyalitas untuk mendapatkan harga itu.”\n"
"\n"
"## Memahami Promosi dan Diskon\n"
"\n"
"Toko sering menggunakan bahasa promosi yang mungkin membingungkan.\n"
"\n"
"Penawaran umum meliputi:\n"
"\n"
"- **Beli satu, dapat satu gratis**\n"
"- **Dua untuk lima**\n"
"- **Diskon dua puluh persen**\n"
"- **Harga dikurangi**\n"
"- **Penawaran spesial**\n"
"- **Harga anggota**\n"
"- **Harga kartu loyalitas**\n"
"- **Obral**\n"
"- **Berlaku hingga Jumat**\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan yang bisa Anda ajukan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah produk ini sedang diskon?”\n"
"- “Bagaimana cara kerja promo ini?”\n"
"- “Apakah saya perlu membeli dua?”\n"
"- “Apakah saya perlu kartu loyalitas?”\n"
"- “Apakah diskonnya diterapkan secara otomatis?”\n"
"- “Kapan promo ini berakhir?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya menggabungkan penawaran ini dengan diskon lain?”\n"
"\n"
"Misalnya:\n"
"\n"
"> “Labelnya mengatakan dua untuk lima. Bisakah saya membeli hanya satu?”\n"
"\n"
"Pegawai bisa menjelaskan:\n"
"\n"
"> “Ya, tetapi satu item akan dikenakan biaya tiga.”\n"
"\n"
"## Bandingkan Produk\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin ingin membandingkan merek, ukuran, bahan, atau harga.\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan yang berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apa perbedaan antara keduanya?”\n"
"- “Yang mana yang lebih populer?”\n"
"- “Yang mana yang lebih baik nilainya?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada opsi yang lebih murah?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda memiliki ukuran yang lebih besar?”\n"
"- “Apakah ini tersedia dalam paket yang lebih kecil?”\n"
"- “Merek mana yang Anda rekomendasikan?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada versi merek toko?”\n"
"\n"
"Frasa yang berguna adalah:\n"
"\n"
"> “Saya mencari sesuatu yang serupa, tetapi lebih murah.”\n"
"\n"
"Anda juga dapat menjelaskan prioritas Anda:\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya butuh sesuatu tanpa gula tambahan.”\n"
"- “Saya mencari opsi berprotein tinggi.”\n"
"- “Saya lebih suka yang organik.”\n"
"- “Saya butuh produk yang akan bertahan beberapa hari.”\n"
"- “Saya mencari nilai terbaik, bukan produk termurah.”\n"
"\n"
"## Tanya Tentang Bahan dan Kebutuhan Diet\n"
"\n"
"Memeriksa bahan sangat penting jika Anda memiliki alergi atau preferensi "
"diet.\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan yang berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah ini mengandung kacang?”\n"
"- “Apakah ini bebas gluten?”\n"
"- “Apakah ini cocok untuk vegetarian?”\n"
"- “Apakah ini vegan?”\n"
"- “Apakah ini mengandung susu?”\n"
"- “Apakah ada gula tambahan?”\n"
"- “Di mana saya bisa menemukan produk bebas laktosa?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda memiliki alternatif tanpa susu?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda juga bisa mengatakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya alergi terhadap kacang tanah.”\n"
"- “Saya tidak bisa makan gluten.”\n"
"- “Saya mencari sesuatu tanpa susu.”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda membantu saya memeriksa bahan-bahannya?”\n"
"\n"
"Untuk alergi serius, selalu baca kemasan dengan hati-hati. Pegawai toko "
"mungkin membantu Anda menemukan informasi, tetapi mereka mungkin tidak bisa "
"menjamin bahwa produk benar-benar bebas alergen.\n"
"\n"
"## Membeli Buah, Sayuran, Daging, atau Keju\n"
"\n"
"Beberapa produk dijual berdasarkan berat daripada paket.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa yang berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya mau satu kilogram apel, tolong.”\n"
"- “Bisa saya dapatkan setengah kilogram tomat?”\n"
"- “Saya mau tiga ratus gram keju.”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda memberi saya enam irisan?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya mendapatkan dua dada ayam?”\n"
"- “Cukup, terima kasih.”\n"
"\n"
"Pegawai mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Berapa banyak yang Anda inginkan?”\n"
"- “Apakah jumlah ini cukup?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda mau diiris?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda mau yang lain?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda perlu kantong?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda bisa menjawab:\n"
"\n"
"- “Sedikit lebih banyak, tolong.”\n"
"- “Sedikit lebih sedikit, tolong.”\n"
"- “Jumlah itu sempurna.”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda mengirisnya tipis?”\n"
"- “Tidak, itu saja.”\n"
"\n"
"## Tanya Tentang Kesegaran Produk\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin ingin memeriksa apakah makanan segar atau berapa lama akan "
"bertahan.\n"
"\n"
"Pertanyaan yang berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Kapan ini kadaluarsa?”\n"
"- “Apa tanggal penggunaannya?”\n"
"- “Apakah ini dipanggang hari ini?”\n"
"- “Apakah ini segar?”\n"
"- “Berapa lama ini bisa bertahan?”\n"
"- “Haruskah saya menyimpan ini di kulkas?”\n"
"- “Bisakah ini dibekukan?”\n"
"\n"
"Label tanggal umum termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- **Sebaiknya sebelum** — produk dapat kehilangan kualitas setelah tanggal "
"ini\n"
"- **Gunakan sebelum** — produk harus dikonsumsi sebelum tanggal ini\n"
"- **Dikemas pada** — tanggal produk dikemas\n"
"- **Jual pada** — tanggal yang terutama digunakan oleh toko\n"
"\n"
"## Menangani Masalah dengan Produk\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin melihat bahwa sebuah item rusak, terbuka, kadaluarsa, atau "
"dilabeli secara salah.\n"
"\n"
"Anda bisa mengatakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Kemasan ini rusak.”\n"
"- “Botol ini bocor.”\n"
"- “Saya pikir produk ini sudah kadaluarsa.”\n"
"- “Segelnya rusak.”\n"
"- “Item ini ada di rak yang salah.”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya menukarkan ini dengan yang lain?”\n"
"- “Bisakah seseorang memeriksa produk ini?”\n"
"\n"
"Tetap sopan dan jelaskan masalahnya dengan jelas.\n"
"\n"
"Misalnya:\n"
"\n"
"> “Permisi, karton ini bocor. Bisakah saya menggantinya?”\n"
"\n"
"## Berbicara di Kasir\n"
"\n"
"Saat Anda sampai di kasir, kasir mungkin menanyakan beberapa pertanyaan "
"umum:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah Anda menemukan semua yang Anda butuhkan?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda memiliki kartu loyalitas?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda mau kantong?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda butuh struk?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda membayar dengan tunai atau kartu?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda mau menyumbang ke amal?”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda butuh bantuan mengepak?”\n"
"\n"
"Jawaban yang berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Ya, saya menemukan semuanya, terima kasih.”\n"
"- “Tidak, saya tidak menemukan satu item.”\n"
"- “Saya tidak punya kartu loyalitas.”\n"
"- “Ya, satu kantong, tolong.”\n"
"- “Tidak perlu kantong, terima kasih.”\n"
"- “Saya akan membayar dengan kartu.”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya mendapatkan struknya, tolong?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya membayar secara terpisah untuk item-item ini?”\n"
"\n"
"## Memahami Instruksi di Kasir\n"
"\n"
"Saat membayar dengan kartu, Anda mungkin mendengar:\n"
"\n"
"- “Silakan masukkan kartu Anda.”\n"
"- “Anda bisa mengetuk kartu Anda.”\n"
"- “Masukkan PIN Anda.”\n"
"- “Pembayaran Anda ditolak.”\n"
"- “Apakah Anda mau mencoba lagi?”\n"
"- “Silakan lepaskan kartu Anda.”\n"
"- “Pembayaran telah berhasil.”\n"
"\n"
"Jika sesuatu salah, Anda bisa mengatakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bisakah saya mencoba kartu lain?”\n"
"- “Bisakah saya membayar dengan tunai saja?”\n"
"- “Saya pikir saya dibebankan dua kali.”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda memeriksa totalnya?”\n"
"- “Harga di rak berbeda.”\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda menghapus item ini, tolong?”\n"
"\n"
"## Menggunakan Kasir Mandiri\n"
"\n"
"Di kasir mandiri, Anda mungkin perlu bertanya kepada seorang pegawai untuk "
"bantuan.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa yang berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bisakah Anda membantu saya dengan kasir mandiri?”\n"
"- “Mesin ini tidak memindai item ini.”\n"
"- “Ini mengatakan ada item tak terduga.”\n"
"- “Bagaimana saya menimbang sayuran?”\n"
"- “Di mana saya memasukkan nomor produk?”\n"
"- “Bagaimana cara menghapus item?”\n"
"- “Mesin ini belum mencetak struk saya.”\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin melihat atau mendengar instruksi seperti:\n"
"\n"
"- “Pindai item pertama Anda.”\n"
"- “Letakkan item di area pengepakan.”\n"
"- “Pilih metode pembayaran Anda.”\n"
"- “Persetujuan diperlukan.”\n"
"- “Silakan tunggu untuk bantuan.”\n"
"\n"
"## Percakapan Sederhana di Toko Bahan Makanan\n"
"\n"
"Interaksi yang khas bisa seperti ini:\n"
"\n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Permisi, bisakah Anda membantu saya menemukan susu oat?  \n"
"> **Pegawai:** Tentu. Itu ada di lorong enam, di sebelah susu biasa.  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Terima kasih. Apakah Anda memiliki versi tanpa pemanis?  \n"
"> **Pegawai:** Ya, kami memiliki dua merek. Yang ini sedang diskon.  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Bagaimana cara kerja promo ini?  \n"
"> **Pegawai:** Ini diskon dua puluh persen jika Anda memiliki kartu "
"loyalitas.  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Saya tidak memilikinya. Apakah ada alternatif yang lebih "
"murah?  \n"
"> **Pegawai:** Ya, versi merek toko lebih murah.  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Bagus. Bisakah Anda menunjukkan di mana letaknya?\n"
"\n"
"## Formula Belanja Sederhana\n"
"\n"
"Ketika Anda membutuhkan bantuan, gunakan struktur ini:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Permintaan perhatian:** “Permisi, bisakah Anda membantu saya?”\n"
"2. **Jelaskan apa yang Anda butuhkan:** “Saya mencari beras coklat.”\n"
"3. **Ajukan pertanyaan spesifik:** “Di lorong mana itu berada?”\n"
"4. **Klarifikasi jawaban:** “Apakah Anda bilang lorong tujuh?”\n"
"5. **Terima kasih kepada pegawai:** “Bagus, terima kasih atas bantuan "
"Anda.”\n"
"\n"
"## Skenario Latihan\n"
"\n"
"Dalam permainan peran ini, Anda berbelanja di FreshMart. Pegawai AI akan "
"membantu Anda menemukan produk, menjelaskan harga dan promosi, serta "
"menjawab pertanyaan tentang toko.\n"
"\n"
"Selama percakapan, coba untuk:\n"
"\n"
